Delegate one bounded task to one named child: { agent, task, title }. Children always run in the background and know only the task you write: state the goal, the scope and files, and the output you need. A child costs a fresh context and returns only its report: do a handful of tool calls or a known lookup yourself, and when in doubt, don't launch. One writer owns each write scope; do not give concurrent children the same files or worktree.

